{
  "id": 3,
  "name": "return_regret_hybrid",
  "intent": "Combines the parent's return-aware bias with a mild regret term so candidates whose alternative options are scarce (high regret) are visited sooner. This targets the grid family's tendency to create zig-zag patterns when nearest-neighbor commits late to a direction, while preserving the return-distance boost that helps clustered instances spread the tour. The regret weight is kept small so raw distance still dominates, avoiding overcommitment to dead-end branches.",
